{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/writingavendordestination"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Writing a Vendor Destination","role":"article"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Send events to an analytics vendor Traffluent doesn’t cover yet, from a module of your own, with the same rules as the destinations it ships.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WritingAVendorDestination"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides"}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A vendor destination is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" with an encoder that writes the vendor’s ingestion"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" already does the batching, retries, drop reports and trace context, so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vendor module adds three things:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"an encoder, a "},{"code":"BatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that writes each record as the vendor’s JSON and splits a batch to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the vendor’s limits;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"a factory on ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that checks what the adopter passes and fills in the endpoint, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder and the limits, so setup is one call;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"tests that run "},{"code":"DestinationTesting","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s conformance checks and compare its requests with recorded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fixtures."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the encoder against the vendor’s public HTTP API, not its SDK, so the app links nothing of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the vendor’s. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":" is built this way and is a full example to copy."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"The-module","type":"heading","text":"The module"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the module depend on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyJSON"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"JSONValues"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlans"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and on swift-distributed-tracing’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Instrumentation"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoOpInstrument"},{"type":"text","text":". Its tests depend on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DestinationTesting"},{"type":"text","text":" as well. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyJSON"},{"type":"text","text":" holds the vendor-neutral pieces an encoder is built"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"JSONValues"},{"type":"text","text":" the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"JSON"},{"type":"text","text":" value it writes, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlans"},{"type":"text","text":" the app’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the encoder reads properties through. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DestinationTesting"},{"type":"text","text":" imports Swift Testing, so it goes in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"test targets only."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".target(name: \"AcmeEncoding\", dependencies: [","    .product(name: \"HTTPDestinations\", package: \"Traffluent\"),","    .product(name: \"PropertyJSON\", package: \"Traffluent\"),","    .product(name: \"JSONValues\", package: \"Traffluent\"),","    .product(name: \"TrackingPlans\", package: \"Traffluent\"),","    .product(name: \"Instrumentation\", package: \"swift-distributed-tracing\"),","]),",".testTarget(name: \"AcmeEncodingTests\", dependencies: [","    \"AcmeEncoding\",","    .product(name: \"DestinationTesting\", package: \"Traffluent\"),","], resources: [.copy(\"Fixtures\")]),"]},{"level":3,"anchor":"The-encoder","type":"heading","text":"The encoder"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The examples here are for Acme, a made-up vendor whose API takes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{\"api_key\": …, \"events\": [{\"event\", \"user_id\", \"insert_id\", \"time\", \"properties\", \"context\"}]}"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and allows at most 500 events and 1,000,000 bytes a request, and 32,000 bytes an event.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyJSON"},{"text":" supplies each piece of such a record:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads an event’s properties through its schema in the app’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaving out "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" values unless you ask for them and the record reveals them."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"EventRecord.standardContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the app, device, locale, network and operating system as JSON,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"code":"flattened(separator:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" turns it into the one level of dotted keys most vendors take.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date.iso8601Timestamp"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date.millisecondsSince1970()"},{"type":"text","text":" are the two timestamp formats vendors"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ask for."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord.pseudonymousIdentity"},{"type":"text","text":" is who the event is about: the record’s session, or the record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"itself when it has none, and never a person ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deduplicationID"},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier a vendor drops repeats by, which a redelivered record keeps."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"BatchLimit.requests(for:in:encoding:oversized:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" splits a batch into requests of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"JSONEnvelope","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" within the vendor’s limits, and leaves out a record that fits in none of them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/\/ Why the Acme encoder left a record out.","enum AcmeEncodingError: Error, Hashable {","    case unreadable(PropertyReadingError)","    case contextKeyCollision(key: String)","    case unrepresentableTimestamp","    case oversized(byteCount: Int)","}","","struct AcmeBatchEncoder: BatchEncoder {","    \/\/\/ Acme's limits on one request.","    static let batchLimit = (try? BatchLimit(maximumRecordCount: 500, maximumByteCount: 1_000_000, maximumRecordByteCount: 32_000)) ?? .unlimited","","    typealias Failure = AcmeEncodingError","","    private let reader: PropertyReader","    private let envelope: JSONEnvelope","","    init(apiKey: String, plan: TrackingPlan) {","        reader = PropertyReader(plan: plan)","        envelope = JSONEnvelope([\"api_key\": .string(apiKey)], arrayMember: \"events\")","    }","","    func requests(for batch: [EventRecord]) -> BatchRequests<AcmeEncodingError> {","        Self.batchLimit.requests(for: batch, in: envelope) { record throws(AcmeEncodingError) in","            try json(of: record)","        } oversized: { byteCount in","            .oversized(byteCount: byteCount)","        }","    }","","    private func json(of record: EventRecord) throws(AcmeEncodingError) -> JSON {","        let properties: [String: JSON]","        do {","            properties = try reader.properties(of: record, includingSensitiveValues: false)","        } catch {","            throw .unreadable(error)","        }","        let context: [String: JSON]","        do {","            context = try record.standardContext.flattened()","        } catch {","            throw .contextKeyCollision(key: error.key)","        }","        let time: Int64","        do {","            time = try record.timestamp.millisecondsSince1970()","        } catch {","            throw .unrepresentableTimestamp","        }","        return .object([","            \"event\": .string(record.name),","            \"user_id\": .string(record.pseudonymousIdentity.uuid.uuidString.lowercased()),","            \"insert_id\": .string(record.deduplicationID),","            \"time\": .integer(time),","            \"properties\": .object(properties),","            \"context\": .object(context),","        ])","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"requests(for:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is all a ","type":"text"},{"code":"BatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" implements, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Failure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" names the reason a record is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left out, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"requests(for:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" doesn’t throw. ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends the requests in order, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reports each record left out as ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"includingSensitiveValues: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only if the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vendor’s terms allow the values, and then only through a factory the adopter opts in with.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the vendor misdates or ignores an event past some age but still answers 2xx, pass an age a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"little short of it to ","type":"text"},{"code":"limit.requests(for:in:maximumAge:encoding:oversized:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which throws","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NegativeMaximumAge","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for one below zero. The spare time covers a request’s trip to the vendor and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"clocks that disagree. Each request then has a deadline that long after its oldest record was","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracked, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drops a request still being retried by then, all of its records, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reports it as ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", rather than send records the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vendor would store wrongly. Have the factory pass its ","type":"text"},{"code":"now:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to both the encoder and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination, so one clock decides what is encoded and what is sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"The-factory","type":"heading","text":"The factory"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The factory is a static method on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" constrained to the encoder, so adopters write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try HTTPDestination.acme(...)"},{"text":". It throws a typed error for input the vendor would refuse, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mistake shows up at launch, not later as a stream of rejected requests. It also takes a transport","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a backoff, which the conformance checks need. It passes ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoOpInstrument()"},{"text":", so no request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"carries the app’s trace context to the vendor, whatever tracer the app bootstraps.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/\/ Why the Acme factory couldn't make a destination.","enum AcmeSetupError: Error, Hashable {","    case emptyAPIKey","    case invalidHost","}","","extension HTTPDestination where Encoding == AcmeBatchEncoder {","    static func acme(","        apiKey: String,","        host: URL,","        plan: TrackingPlan,","        transport: Transport,","        backoff: ExponentialBackoff = ExponentialBackoff()","    ) throws(AcmeSetupError) -> HTTPDestination<Transport, AcmeBatchEncoder> {","        guard !apiKey.isEmpty else { throw .emptyAPIKey }","        guard host.scheme == \"https\", host.host() != nil else { throw .invalidHost }","        return HTTPDestination(","            endpoint: host.appending(path: \"v1\/events\"),","            \/\/ Acme doesn't read a trace context, so the app's traces aren't sent to it.","            instrument: NoOpInstrument(),","            transport: transport,","            encoder: AcmeBatchEncoder(apiKey: apiKey, plan: plan),","            backoff: backoff)","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Offer an overload without "},{"code":"transport:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that passes "},{"code":"URLSessionTransport()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as PostHog’s does, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an app needn’t name one."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"The-conformance-checks","type":"heading","text":"The conformance checks"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DestinationConformance"},{"type":"text","text":" runs the checks every vendor destination must pass. Give it the vendor’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"limit and a closure that calls the factory with the setup’s plan, transport and backoff:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck\/sensitiveValuesRedacted","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": no ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is sent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without the adopter’s opt-in.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck\/consentHolds","type":"reference"},{"text":": behind consent and ","type":"text"},{"code":"accepting(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination sends exactly the records it is handed.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck\/oversizedRecordSkipped","isActive":true},{"text":": a record over the limit is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"skipped and reported.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck\/transientFailuresRetried","type":"reference"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck\/rejectionsDropped","type":"reference"},{"text":": failures are retried or dropped as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" classifies them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck\/traceContextWithheld"},{"text":": no request carries a trace context,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"even while a tracer is active.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"expectRequests(of:plan:matchFixture:withExtension:subdirectory:in:sourceLocation:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" compares the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests a hand-worked batch makes with a fixture in the test target’s resources, byte for byte.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"When the fixture is missing, the issue it records holds the requests, so you can check them by hand","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"against the vendor’s documentation and save them as the fixture.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@Test(arguments: ConformanceCheck.allCases)","func acmeConformance(check: ConformanceCheck) async throws {","    let host = try #require(URL(string: \"https:\/\/acme.example.com\"))","    let conformance = DestinationConformance(limit: AcmeBatchEncoder.batchLimit) { setup in","        try HTTPDestination.acme(apiKey: \"test-key\", host: host, plan: setup.plan, transport: setup.transport, backoff: setup.backoff)","    }","    try await conformance.expect(check)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each check records a Swift Testing issue for each rule the destination breaks. The kit is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shared assertion on purpose, so every vendor module runs the same checks. Every check’s records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracked at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setup.timestamp"},{"text":"; if your encoder leaves out records older than the vendor takes, give","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it that as the time it encodes at, as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"},{"text":"’s tests do.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","abstract":[{"text":"Tell the people and services that read your events what each event holds, and hear about a change that would break their data before it ships.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/ConformanceCheck/transientFailuresRetried":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/conformancecheck\/transientfailuresretried","title":"ConformanceCheck.transientFailuresRetried","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck\/transientFailuresRetried","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transientFailuresRetried","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A request that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429 is sent again, byte for byte, until it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered, and nothing is reported."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/ConformanceCheck/sensitiveValuesRedacted":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is never sent by the default destination, even by a record that reveals","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. With the adopter’s opt-in, it is sent while the record reveals it, and not once the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record is redacted.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck\/sensitiveValuesRedacted","url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/conformancecheck\/sensitivevaluesredacted","title":"ConformanceCheck.sensitiveValuesRedacted","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sensitiveValuesRedacted","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Typed analytics events for Swift, delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","title":"Traffluent","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","title":"Automatic Tracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","title":"Sessions and Standard Context","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/ConformanceCheck/oversizedRecordSkipped":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/conformancecheck\/oversizedrecordskipped","title":"ConformanceCheck.oversizedRecordSkipped","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck\/oversizedRecordSkipped","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"oversizedRecordSkipped"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A record too large for the vendor’s limit is left out and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the batch’s other records are sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/ConformanceCheck/consentHolds":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Behind a tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Consent"},{"type":"text","text":" and the destination’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accepting(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the destination sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event of a granted category it accepts, and not the event of a denied category or of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one it doesn’t accept."}],"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/conformancecheck\/consentholds","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck\/consentHolds","title":"ConformanceCheck.consentHolds","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"consentHolds","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","title":"Defining Events","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/IdentifyingPeople":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/identifyingpeople","title":"Identifying People","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent knows people only by a pseudonymous session. An identifier that outlives one is yours to add, store, reset and gate with consent."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/ConformanceCheck/rejectionsDropped":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/conformancecheck\/rejectionsdropped","title":"ConformanceCheck.rejectionsDropped","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck\/rejectionsDropped","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rejectionsDropped","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A request answered with a status retrying won’t change (400, 401, 403, 404, 413, 422) is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent once and reported as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.rejected(status:recordIDs:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/ConformanceCheck/traceContextWithheld":{"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/conformancecheck\/tracecontextwithheld","abstract":[{"text":"No request carries a trace context in its header fields (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traceparent"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracestate"},{"text":", or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever the instrument injects), even while a tracer is active and the record was tracked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in a span: a vendor’s destination passes ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoOpInstrument()"},{"text":", so the app’s traces stay in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the app.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck\/traceContextWithheld","type":"topic","title":"ConformanceCheck.traceContextWithheld","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"traceContextWithheld"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding":{"url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog through its batch capture API.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","type":"topic","title":"PostHogEncoding","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","title":"Persisting Records","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","type":"topic","title":"Consent Gating","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","abstract":[{"text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","type":"topic","title":"Sampling Events","role":"article","kind":"article"}}}